    "availabilityStatus": "The data are very rich and contain information that are highly (privacy-)sensitive for schools and students. For this reason, data cannot be shared publicly without restrictions. \n\nFor privacy issues, schools can never share their own data on students with third parties. Third parties can request access to the teacher- and student- survey data. They can submit a request for a (re-)usage of the data via the WOA (Werkplaats Onderwijsonderzoek Amsterdam), where the researcher and school managements jointly cooperate. The requests will be discussed within the WOA. Data requests will be evaluated on the basis of ethical/privacy considerations (i.e., can data be made accessible without jeopardizing the anonymity of schools, teachers and/or students). Moreover, the data can only be used for purposes that align with, or are in the spirit of, the project’s original purposes and aims for which participant consent was obtained. Data can only be used for purposes that do not interfere with running or planned research projects. ",
    "contactForAccess": "WOA (Werkplaats Onderwijsonderzoek Amsterdam)",
    "sizeOfCollection": "Survey data: 867 students and 133 teachers in 63 schools\nSchool management data: 1033 students in 63 schools\nCBS/NCO data: 1016 students in 63 schools\n",
    "studyCompletion": "school year 2022-2023",
